    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Never for Ever is Kate Bush’s third studio album, released in 1980 on EMI, and it marked a major turning point in her career by becoming her first UK No. 1 album. Musically, it expands her early art-pop sound into a more varied and adventurous mix of rock, pop, progressive pop, and new wave textures, with a stronger role for synthesizers and drum machines, including early Fairlight CMI experimentation.\n\nThe record is often praised for its range and sophistication, moving from the urgent drama of “Babooshka” and “The Wedding List” to the reflective “Army Dreamers” and the powerful closing track “Breathing.” Co-produced by Bush and Jon Kelly, it was also a commercial breakthrough, yielding several UK Top 20 singles and confirming her as one of the most original and ambitious voices in British pop.",
